What was checked and how:

1. Selection equivalence. The old code ran 'any(start < index for start in starts)'
   once per end line. The new code runs 'starts[0] < index' under an 'if starts' guard.
   These are equal for every input, because the start list is ascending, so
   starts[0] is its minimum. Probe review-a-3 loaded the 0b6670d module and the
   33f608d module side by side and compared dispositions_feedback on all 21845 logs
   of length 0 to 7 over a 4-token alphabet, and on 3000 random logs of length 0 to
