2. The new contracts.md text. The end rule says the block ends at the last END line
   that has a MEASURE_AGENT_RESULT line above it. The code takes the last end index
   with starts[0] < index, which is the same rule. The start rule names the last end
   line before the last start line of the block; the code takes floor from
   earlier_ends and then block_starts[0]. Probe cases matched each clause: a start
   line on line 1 starts the block; START / role / x / END / bad / END gives
   feedback (the Review B case); an invalid line above the block start does not
   count; a second start line inside the block cannot hide a line above it; a log
   with no end line gives no feedback; a line after the block end does not count.

3. The docstring. It states the same two rules and the linear-cost sentence. The
